{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Java SDK (U1) and Python SDK (U2) will be developed as new language-specific SDKs following the existing Fabric SDK patterns (similar to Node SDK), providing APIs for identity management, transaction proposal, endorsement, and event listening.",
    "Pre-built chaincode deployment (U3) will be implemented by extending the chaincode lifecycle (install/approve/commit) to accept pre-built container images, requiring changes to the peer's chaincode deployment logic and the fabric-chaintool packaging tool.",
    "VSCC validation logging enhancement (U4) will modify the validation system chaincode and the peer's transaction validator to emit detailed policy evaluation logs at INFO level, including policy structure, signer identities (peer/org), and missing signatures, and will also extend the event service to include this information in validation failure events.",
    "Platform-specific binaries (U5) will be produced by enhancing the existing build system (Makefile/Golang cross-compilation) to generate release artifacts for configtxgen, fabric-chaintool, fabric-ca client, and peer/orderer binaries for Linux (amd64, arm64), macOS (amd64, arm64), and Windows (amd64), and publishing them to GitHub Releases.",
    "Certificate fingerprint pinning (U6) will be implemented as an optional MSP configuration feature: organizations can configure a fingerprint list endpoint (HTTP) or a channel-config-loaded list signed by an organization-controlled key; validation will occur at endorsement time for endpoint-based lists and at commit time for channel-config-loaded lists, with key rollover support via key versioning.",
    "Quick-start testing documentation (U7) will be improved by enhancing the existing fabric/test/network scripts (e.g., byfn.sh, eyfn.sh) and adding comprehensive READMEs, then updating the readthedocs testing page with links and instructions.",
    "Default configuration consolidation (U8) will create a new 'config_defaults' directory in the repository root containing fully commented core.yaml, orderer.yaml, and configtx.yaml with all possible configuration keys and their default values, and update documentation/BYFN to reference this location."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has deep familiarity with Hyperledger Fabric codebase (Go, Java, Python) and its build/release processes.",
    "Existing CI/CD infrastructure (GitHub Actions, Nexus) is available for binary publishing and SDK artifact deployment.",
    "U1 and U2 refer to developing new production-ready SDKs (not just wrappers) with feature parity to the Node SDK at the time of the specification.",
    "Pre-built chaincode (U3) assumes the use of Docker/OCI images as the packaging format and that peers have container runtime access.",
    "VSCC logging (U4) changes are confined to the peer's validation logic and the VSCC system chaincode; no changes to the ordering service.",
    "Certificate fingerprint pinning (U6) will be implemented as an extension to the existing MSP/identity validation flow without requiring a new consensus mechanism.",
    "Quick-start testing (U7) focuses on documentation and script improvements, not on creating new network topologies.",
    "Configuration consolidation (U8) assumes all configuration keys are statically definable in YAML; dynamic defaults derived from code will be documented as comments.",
    "All estimates are for a single experienced developer working full-time (1 workday = 8 hours) with no parallelization.",
    "Integration testing effort is included within each feature's testing activities; no separate end-to-end integration phase is estimated."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Java SDK Design & Architecture",
      "activity_description": "Define Java SDK API surface, module structure, dependency management (Maven/Gradle), and alignment with Fabric gateway model.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Java SDK Core Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement connection management, identity/wallet, transaction proposal creation, endorsement handling, commit status listening, and event streaming.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Java SDK Unit Tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for all SDK modules using JUnit/Mockito, targeting >80% coverage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Java SDK Integration Tests",
      "activity_description": "Develop integration tests against a running Fabric network (using test network scripts) for end-to-end scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Java SDK Documentation & Examples",
      "activity_description": "Create API docs (Javadoc), getting started guide, and sample applications.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Python SDK Design & Architecture",
      "activity_description": "Define Python SDK API, packaging (setuptools/pyproject.toml), async/sync support, and compatibility with Fabric gateway.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Python SDK Core Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Implement gRPC client, identity management, transaction flow, event listening, and error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Python SDK Unit Tests",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests with pytest/mock, targeting >80% coverage.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Python SDK Integration Tests",
      "activity_description": "Develop integration tests against Fabric test network for key scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Python SDK Documentation & Examples",
      "activity_description": "Create Sphinx docs, README, and sample applications.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Pre-built Chaincode Design",
      "activity_description": "Design chaincode package format (OCI image with metadata), lifecycle extensions (install/approve/commit), and peer deployment flow.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "fabric-chaintool Enhancements",
      "activity_description": "Extend fabric-chaintool to build and package chaincode as OCI images with required metadata (labels, entrypoint).",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A13",
      "activity_name": "Peer Chaincode Deployment Changes",
      "activity_description": "Modify peer's chaincode lifecycle (lifecycle/chaincode.go) to pull and run pre-built images instead of building from source.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A14",
      "activity_name": "Chaincode Lifecycle Updates",
      "activity_description": "Update lifecycle commands (peer lifecycle chaincode) to accept package IDs referencing pre-built images and handle approval/commit.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A15",
      "activity_name": "Pre-built Chaincode Testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit and integration tests for packaging, installation, approval, commit, and invocation of pre-built chaincode.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A16",
      "activity_name": "VSCC Logging Analysis",
      "activity_description": "Analyze current VSCC validation code and log output to identify gaps in policy/signer information.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A17",
      "activity_name": "VSCC Enhanced Logging Design",
      "activity_description": "Design log format and event structure to include policy tree, signer identities (peer/org), satisfied/missing principals.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A18",
      "activity_name": "VSCC & Validator Implementation",
      "activity_description": "Modify VSCC (vscc.go) and txvalidator to emit detailed INFO logs and populate validation failure events with policy/signer details.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A19",
      "activity_name": "Event Service Extension",
      "activity_description": "Extend block/transaction event service to include validation failure details for SDK consumers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A20",
      "activity_name": "VSCC Logging Testing",
      "activity_description": "Test logging output for various policy types (AND, OR, NOutOf) and signer combinations; verify event content.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A21",
      "activity_name": "Cross-compilation Build Setup",
      "activity_description": "Configure Go cross-compilation toolchains for target platforms (Linux amd64/arm64, macOS amd64/arm64, Windows amd64) in CI.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A22",
      "activity_name": "Build Scripts for Tools",
      "activity_description": "Create/update Makefile targets and release scripts to build configtxgen, fabric-chaintool, fabric-ca client, peer, orderer for all platforms.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A23",
      "activity_name": "Binary Packaging & Publishing",
      "activity_description": "Package binaries into archives (tar.gz, zip), generate checksums, and publish to GitHub Releases with versioned tags.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A24",
      "activity_name": "Binary Documentation Updates",
      "activity_description": "Update installation docs, BYFN, and readthedocs to reference pre-built binaries and verify download links.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A25",
      "activity_name": "Binary Verification Testing",
      "activity_description": "Smoke test each binary on each platform to ensure they execute and produce expected help/version output.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A26",
      "activity_name": "Certificate Pinning Design",
      "activity_description": "Design MSP configuration schema for fingerprint lists (endpoint URL or channel-config key), validation points (endorsement vs commit), and key rollover mechanism.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A27",
      "activity_name": "Endorsement-time Fingerprint Retrieval",
      "activity_description": "Implement HTTP client in peer to fetch fingerprint lists from configured endpoints during endorsement, with caching and error handling.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A28",
      "activity_name": "Channel-config Fingerprint List Loading",
      "activity_description": "Extend channel configuration to include organization-signed fingerprint lists; implement validation at commit time using loaded lists.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A29",
      "activity_name": "MSP Validation Integration",
      "activity_description": "Integrate fingerprint checking into MSP identity validation (ValidateIdentity) for both endorsement and commit paths.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A30",
      "activity_name": "Key Rollover & Loss Handling",
      "activity_description": "Implement key versioning in channel config, support for multiple active keys, and procedures for key compromise/recovery.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A31",
      "activity_name": "Certificate Pinning Testing",
      "activity_description": "Unit tests for fingerprint matching, integration tests for endorsement/commit validation with both mechanisms, and key rollover scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A32",
      "activity_name": "Test Network Script Enhancements",
      "activity_description": "Improve byfn.sh/eyfn.sh and related scripts for faster startup, configurable profiles, and better error reporting.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A33",
      "activity_name": "Testing Documentation & ReadTheDocs",
      "activity_description": "Write comprehensive testing guide (readthedocs/testing.html) with links to script READMEs, chaincode examples, and troubleshooting.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A34",
      "activity_name": "Example Chaincode Projects",
      "activity_description": "Create sample chaincode projects (Go, Java, JavaScript) with build/deploy instructions for quick testing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A35",
      "activity_name": "Quick-start Validation",
      "activity_description": "Execute quick-start procedures on clean environments to verify documentation accuracy and script reliability.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A36",
      "activity_name": "Configuration Audit",
      "activity_description": "Scan peer, orderer, and configtx source code to inventory all configuration keys, defaults, and environment variable overrides.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A37",
      "activity_name": "Config Defaults Directory Creation",
      "activity_description": "Create config_defaults/ directory with core.yaml, orderer.yaml, configtx.yaml templates containing all keys and descriptive comments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A38",
      "activity_name": "Default Configuration Generation",
      "activity_description": "Populate configuration files with every known key and its default value; ensure parity with code defaults.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A39",
      "activity_name": "Documentation & BYFN Updates",
      "activity_description": "Update configuration documentation, BYFN instructions, and readthedocs to reference config_defaults as the single source of truth.",
